<!--
  The periodic background agent.

  A separate assembly because Windows Phone loads agents into their own process:
  the app cannot simply schedule one of its own methods. It shares Core and the
  phone-specific shims by linking the same source files, so there is one
  implementation of the protocol rather than two that drift.

  No manifest of its own - the app's WMAppManifest declares it through an
  ExtendedTask/BackgroundServiceAgent entry naming the type below.
-->
